### Description

Update the specified job template.

**The request body describes the desired final state of the template, not an incremental patch.** Existing steps that
are absent from `step_list` are deleted, and existing global variables that are absent from `global_var_list` are
deleted. The recommended usage is to read the current configuration with `get_job_template_detail`, modify it and
write the whole thing back.

Prerequisites: the job template exists in the scope; the caller has permission to edit it, and holds the
corresponding view/use permissions on every referenced resource (scripts, file sources, accounts). When `name` is
provided, template names must be unique within the same resource scope.

Three cases for the step `id`:

- **An existing step ID**: the step is kept and updated with the request content; its ID stays unchanged
- **Omitted (absent or null)**: treated as a new step; the server assigns an ID
- **The step is not listed at all**: the step is removed from the template

Non-positive values such as `-1` and `0` are rejected. A step ID that does not belong to this template results in a
parameter error naming that ID. Step IDs must be unique within one request.

Global variables are matched by `name`: a matching name updates the existing variable, and existing variables that
are absent are deleted. **Renaming is not supported** — a rename is equivalent to deleting the old variable and
adding a new one, which loses the value the variable holds in derived job plans.

The array order of `step_list` is the execution order; reordering the array reorders the steps without changing step
IDs.

After a template update, job plans derived from it are marked as pending sync (`need_update=true`), but their own
configuration is not changed automatically. Call `sync_job_plan` to bring a plan up to date.

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field           | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                                           |
|-----------------|--------|----------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| bk_scope_type   | string | Yes      | Resource scope type. Allowed values: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set)                                                       |
| bk_scope_id     | string | Yes      | Resource scope ID matching `bk_scope_type` (business ID or business set ID)                                                           |
| id              | long   | Yes      | Job template ID; must be greater than 0; the template must exist                                                                      |
| name            | string | No       | Job template name. Omit it or leave it blank to keep the current name; when provided it must be 1–60 characters, must not contain HTML special characters `<`, `>`, `"`, `'`, and must be unique within the same scope |
| description     | string | No       | Job template description, up to 500 characters                                                                                        |
| global_var_list | array  | No       | Global variable list; existing variables absent from this list are deleted; variable names must be unique within one request          |
| step_list       | array  | Yes      | Job step list; the array order is the execution order; must be non-empty; existing steps absent from this list are deleted            |

Template tags are out of scope for this API; the existing tags of the template are kept as they are.

##### global_var_list[] element

{% include '_generic_v4_template_global_var_req.md.j2' %}

##### step_list[] element

| Field         | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                       |
|---------------|--------|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| id            | long   | No       | Step ID. An existing step ID keeps and updates that step; omitting it adds a new step; `-1`, `0` and other non-positive values are rejected |
| name          | string | Yes      | Step name, 1–60 characters; must not contain HTML special characters `<`, `>`, `"`, `'`                           |
| type          | int    | Yes      | Step type. Allowed values: `1` (script execution), `2` (file transfer), `3` (manual confirmation)                 |
| script_info   | object | No       | Script step detail. Required when `type` is 1                                                                     |
| file_info     | object | No       | File transfer step detail. Required when `type` is 2                                                              |
| approval_info | object | No       | Manual confirmation step detail. Required when `type` is 3                                                        |

{% include '_generic_v4_template_step_req.md.j2' %}

##### account

| Field       | Type   | Required | Description                                                                          |
|-------------|--------|----------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| id          | long   | No       | Account ID. Mutually exclusive with `account_var`; `id` wins when both are given     |
| account_var | string | No       | Name of a global variable of type "execute account" to reference. Mutually exclusive with `id` |

At least one of `id` and `account_var` must be provided.

##### execute_target

{% include '_generic_v4_template_execute_target_req.md.j2' %}

### Request Example

The example below turns the existing steps `101`, `102`, `103` into "keep 101, delete 102, keep 103 and append a new
manual confirmation step".

- POST

```json
{
    "bk_scope_type": "biz",
    "bk_scope_id": "2",
    "id": 1000,
    "name": "my-api-template",
    "description": "updated by openapi",
    "global_var_list": [
        {
            "name": "TARGET_DIR",
            "type": 1,
            "required": 1,
            "value": "/data/release-v2"
        }
    ],
    "step_list": [
        {
            "id": 101,
            "name": "run-script",
            "type": 1,
            "script_info": {
                "script_type": 2,
                "script_id": "3a1b0e8f9c2d4e5f",
                "script_version_id": 5001,
                "script_timeout": 1000,
                "account": {
                    "id": 1
                },
                "execute_target": {
                    "host_list": [
                        {
                            "bk_host_id": 10001
                        }
                    ]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 103,
            "name": "transfer-file",
            "type": 2,
            "file_info": {
                "file_source_list": [
                    {
                        "file_type": 3,
                        "file_list": [
                            "/bucket/config.yaml"
                        ],
                        "file_source_id": 7
                    }
                ],
                "file_destination": {
                    "path": "/data/release",
                    "account": {
                        "id": 1
                    },
                    "execute_target": {
                        "host_list": [
                            {
                                "bk_host_id": 10001
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "confirm",
            "type": 3,
            "approval_info": {
                "approval_user": {
                    "user_list": [
                        "admin"
                    ]
                },
                "approval_message": "confirm to release"
            }
        }
    ]
}
```

